WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.743
SQL is not just INT and TEXT.

00:00:07.743 --> 00:00:13.486
One engine queries maps, documents, DNA, and even an LLM, all through the same SELECT, FROM, WHERE.

00:00:13.486 --> 00:00:19.229
So you reach for a specialized database far later than you think.

00:00:19.229 --> 00:00:22.705
The query shape never changes.

00:00:22.705 --> 00:00:26.182
SELECT, FROM, WHERE, ORDER BY.

00:00:26.182 --> 00:00:29.658
Geographic queries test points within five kilometers, right in the WHERE.

00:00:29.658 --> 00:00:33.135
Genomic work runs edit distance on DNA.

00:00:33.135 --> 00:00:36.611
A flexible document is just a JSON column.

00:00:36.611 --> 00:00:40.088
And generative AI calls an LLM over each row.

00:00:40.088 --> 00:00:43.564
Same query, a new function each time.

00:00:43.564 --> 00:00:47.699
A little JSON, so you need a NoSQL cluster?

00:00:47.699 --> 00:00:51.834
No.

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:55.968
One Postgres node with a JSON column gives you flexible documents plus ACID and joins.

00:00:55.968 --> 00:01:00.103
That carries an MVP far past where teams think they need MongoDB.

00:01:00.103 --> 00:01:05.057
The newest type is the model itself.

00:01:05.057 --> 00:01:10.010
One function runs an LLM over a column.

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:14.964
Tag a song's mood, summarize its lyrics, translate its title, all in the same query that filters and sorts the rows.

00:01:14.964 --> 00:01:19.713
Every decade SQL added a type, never a new language.

00:01:19.713 --> 00:01:24.461
Numbers, then dates, then JSON, now vectors and LLM calls.

00:01:24.461 --> 00:01:29.209
The SELECT, FROM, WHERE you know already reaches them.

00:01:29.209 --> 00:01:33.958
Next, what happens when one node is finally not enough.
